# build/config.yml
#
# Wails v3 project metadata. The real `wails3` build system (Task +
# these generated Taskfiles) reads this when producing icons, platform
# manifests (macOS Info.plist / Windows build/windows/info.json), and
# installers — see https://v3.wails.io/concepts/build-system/ and
# https://v3.wails.io/guides/cli/ (the `-config` flag on `wails3 dev`
# defaults to exactly this path).
#
# HONESTY NOTE (see README's Phase 13 section for the full context):
# this file was hand-authored against Wails v3's own documented example
# structure, NOT generated or validated by a real `wails3 init` /
# `wails3 generate` run — the CLI requires Go >= 1.25, which this
# sandbox cannot obtain (apt's newest package is 1.24, and Go's own
# toolchain auto-fetch is blocked by network policy — both confirmed
# empirically, not assumed). Treat the field VALUES below as accurate
# (they're real project facts, not placeholders) but treat the file's
# mere existence as scaffolding for whoever next has real `wails3`
# tooling to verify and extend, not as proof packaging has been tested.
#
# version stays unprefixed ("0.1.0", not "v0.1.0") — Wails' own NSIS
# packaging step requires a plain numeric version string.

